# Users allowed to ask the Hermes session broker for client accounts.
#
# One name or numeric uid per line; '#' starts a comment. The uid is taken
# from the kernel through SO_PEERCRED, so an entry here grants exactly the
# account that runs Hermes and nobody who can merely reach the socket.
#
# Grant this to the user Hermes runs as. Everything that user can then ask for
# is bounded by the broker's requests: it cannot name an account, choose a uid,
# or reach outside the session home root. START does let it choose the command
# a session runs, which is not an escalation - the command runs as the session
# account, which holds strictly less than the Hermes user already does - but it
# is the reason this file lists the Hermes user and nobody else.
